{
  "success": true,
  "data": [
    {
      "descriptor": "{
  "_comment": "Phase-4 real-device validation descriptor for the network-provisioning pipeline. The Harvester FETCHES this from its raw GitHub URL (https://raw.githubusercontent.com/paichart/paichart/main/descriptors/ceos-lab-readonly-descriptor.json) — put that URL in the pipeline task description. It points at sydasif/nornir-mcp-server fronting a Arista cEOS lab (2-node or the igp-triangle 3-node variant) on prod, reachable at the STABLE named cloudflared tunnel ceos-lab.paichart.app (systemd service on prod → localhost:3107). Declares the READ-ONLY harvest subset: list_devices + fetch_data(NAPALM getters) + show_commands CONSTRAINED to an enumerated allowlist of state-read commands (added 2026-08-23 after IGP-T1 R6's P2 leg correctly ESCALATED: zero-tolerance route parity was unverifiable because NAPALM has no route-table/IGP-adjacency getter). The SERVICE's show_commands accepts arbitrary strings — the enum below is descriptor-level scoping, the same restriction model as the rest of this file (not service-level R1 enforcement). apply_config/backup_configs remain deliberately NOT declared. All allowlisted commands except 'show ip route isis' were live-verified on EOS 4.32.2.1F during the IGP-T1 window; 'show ip route' is the guaranteed superset fallback. HONEST CAVEAT: nornir-mcp authenticates to the device with STATIC creds, NOT the JWKS-forwarded identity WS4 R2a mandates — so this is NOT WS4-conformant. It validates the COGNITION pipeline (harvest -> design -> change-package vs REAL EOS) + R9-at-the-wire, not the identity contract. Rig + runbook: copov15 .claude/knowledge/pipelines/network-provisioning/phase4-ceos-rig/.",
  "name": "ceos-lab-readonly",
  "description": "Read-only Arista EOS network-state harvest for the network-provisioning pipeline. Exposes list_devices, fetch_data (NAPALM getters: running-config, interfaces, facts, BGP neighbors, etc.), and show_commands restricted to an enumerated allowlist of state-read commands (route tables, OSPF/IS-IS neighbors, IS-IS hostname map) against a cEOS lab. Authenticates to devices with a static service credential (validation rig; not JWKS per-user identity). No preconditions; call fetch_data with getter names, or show_commands with allowlisted commands.",
  "endpoint": "https://ceos-lab.paichart.app/mcp",
  "category": "automation",
  "version": "0.3.0",
  "capabilities": {
    "transport": "streamable-http",
    "tools": [
      {
        "name": "list_devices",
        "description": "List network devices and inventory (devices, groups, or both). Read-only. Call this first to discover device names before fetch_data.",
        "inputSchema": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "query_type": {
              "type": "string",
              "enum": [
                "devices",
                "groups",
                "all"
              ],
              "default": "all",
              "description": "Inventory data to return: 'devices', 'groups', or 'all'"
            },
            "details": {
              "type": "boolean",
              "default": false,
              "description": "Return full device attributes (for a devices query)"
            },
            "filter_name": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Filter by inventory device name (e.g. 'ceos1')"
            },
            "filter_hostname": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Filter by hostname / IP"
            },
            "filter_group": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Filter by group (e.g. 'arista_eos')"
            },
            "filter_platform": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Filter by platform (e.g. 'eos')"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "fetch_data",
        "description": "Execute one or more READ-ONLY NAPALM getters against the EOS devices and return structured state (running-config, interfaces, facts, BGP neighbors, etc.). This is the Phase-0 harvest surface. Read-only by construction — NAPALM getters never mutate device state.",
        "inputSchema": {
          "type": "object",
          "required": [
            "getters"
          ],
          "properties": {
            "getters": {
              "type": "array",
              "description": "NAPALM getter names to run (short form, no 'get_' prefix). All entries are read-only EOS getters.",
              "minItems": 1,
              "items": {
                "type": "string",
                "enum": [
                  "config",
                  "facts",
                  "interfaces",
                  "interfaces_ip",
                  "interfaces_counters",
                  "lldp_neighbors",
                  "lldp_neighbors_detail",
                  "bgp_neighbors",
                  "bgp_config",
                  "environment",
                  "arp_table",
                  "mac_address_table",
                  "ntp_servers",
                  "snmp_information",
                  "users",
                  "optics",
                  "network_instances"
                ]
              }
            },
            "getters_options": {
              "type": "object",
              "description": "Optional per-getter options, e.g. {\"config\": {\"retrieve\": \"running\"}}.",
              "additionalProperties": true
            },
            "filter_name": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Restrict to one inventory device name (e.g. 'ceos1')"
            },
            "filter_hostname": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Restrict by hostname / IP"
            },
            "filter_group": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Restrict by group"
            },
            "filter_platform": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Restrict by platform"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "show_commands",
        "description": "Execute READ-ONLY operational 'show' commands from the enumerated allowlist below and return raw CLI output. Added for route-table, IGP-adjacency and link-state-database state that NAPALM getters cannot retrieve (parity verification, neighbour baselines). NOTE on parity during protocol coexistence: while one IGP is administratively preferred, the other's routes are computed but NOT installed, so routing-table views show them as absent even on a healthy fabric — the link-state database is where that evidence lives. Commands outside the allowlist are not part of this service's declared surface — do not send them.",
        "inputSchema": {
          "type": "object",
          "required": [
            "commands"
          ],
          "properties": {
            "commands": {
              "type": "array",
              "minItems": 1,
              "description": "Allowlisted read-only show commands to run on the filtered devices.",
              "items": {
                "type": "string",
                "enum": [
                  "show ip route",
                  "show ip route ospf",
                  "show ip route isis",
                  "show ip ospf neighbor",
                  "show isis neighbor",
                  "show isis hostname",
                  "show ip ospf interface brief",
                  "show isis database",
                  "show isis database detail"
                ]
              }
            },
            "filter_name": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Restrict to one inventory device name (e.g. 'ceos1')"
            },
            "filter_hostname": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Restrict by hostname / IP"
            },
            "filter_group": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Restrict by group"
            },
            "filter_platform": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Restrict by platform"
            }
          }
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}
"
    }
  ],
  "pageCount": 1,
  "timing": {
    "startTime": "2026-08-27T01:04:30.057Z",
    "endTime": "2026-08-27T01:04:30.920Z",
    "durationMs": 863
  }
}
